	{
	"id": "foe.ostlingant",
	"description": "Minor servants of the Aviform Hours, known as secret-carriers and minstrel-deceivers. They do not fly by daylight - nor anywhere in the waking world, for that matter - and their songs are not meant for mortal ears. [If this Enemy's attack goes undefended, it will inflict Trauma upon you. Killing this enemy may get you closer to the ragged sword.]"
	},
	
	{
	"id": "foe.voice",
	"description": "'Turn back, turn back...' [If this Enemy's attack goes undefended, it will destroy Whispers on Wings if one can be found. Killing this enemy may get you closer to the ragged sword.]"
	},
	
	{
	"id": "foe.grame",
	"description": "If wolf-splinters are the soul's despair outpacing its light, and wrakes the agonies that consume the spirit, then wolf-grames are the simmering, festering rage of the unavenged and unanswered. I must be host to dozens. [Killing this enemy may help you complete your purpose here.]",
	},
	
	{
	"id": "foe.shade",
	"description": "'Are you not tired? Come, come. Walk with us on the road that knows no sun nor moon; no pain nor grief; no here nor there. Come, and there will be no more.' [Whenever this Enemy acts, there is a chance for it produce Mounting Dread. Killing this enemy may help you complete your purpose here.]",
	},
	
